    "body": "\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\nAn insert-session (`mc_ins_cascade_start`) saves a preliminary \"covering\" undo-entry, to cover all cursors. If the insert-session exits without changes, that no-op entry remains, requiring an extra \"u\".\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nDrop the entry at insert-session end if there were no changes.\r\n\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41883\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-18T13:57:52Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41979#discussion_r4047039616"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/41979"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4047039616"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This \"start a covering undo block\" approach feels nicer than storing a flag and adding undo in just the right place later. \r\n\r\nBut this means the \"empty undo entry\" case needs to be dropped later, and that's why this PR adds `u_forget_unchanged`. \r\n\r\nThat model is similar to how 'inccommand' works (undo-and-forget), except inccommand forgets the whole undo branch instead of just an empty \"entry\".\r\n",
            "commit_id": "5bab0cdde8e96438ed08435e7bb095db72a604a2",
            "created_at": "2026-09-18T13:14:35Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -605,8 +605,9 @@ void mc_ins_cascade_start(bool cascade, varnumber_T tick)\n \n   if (mc_ins_span.active) {\n     // Cover the line-range of all cursors with one undo-entry. #41822\n+    // If the insert-session changes nothing, mc_ins_commit() drops it. #41883\n     //\n-    // Undo entries apply in reverse save-order, so this entry (saved first) \"wins\", even though\n+    // Undo entries apply in reverse save-order, so this (first) entry \"wins\", even though\n     // per-cursor newline-shifting edits may record conflicting undo entries. Same approach is used\n     // by Vim for linewise-op/range-command (see u_save in op_shift, ex_sort, …).",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41979#discussion_r4047039616",
            "id": 4047039616,
            "line": 612,
            "node_id": "PRRC_kwDOAPphoM7xOOyA",
